comments[5]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-06T05:10:46.180Z",codex-agent,"Exact fractions, finite unit conversions, semantic and population refusals, conservative intervals and unknown propagation are implemented. All authoritative records and replay identities are in native unit_state with native comments and related links. Ten behavioral safeguard removals fail in disposable copies; the restored implementation passes. One linked run caught stale dist after new pure-API validation was added; the final linked command will include a fresh build."
  "2026-11-06T05:20:59.179Z",codex-agent,"The linked npm run test:core now builds first and passes 6 of 6 tests through pm test. The native-directory adapter preserves active extension schema and chooses field versus project-schema options dynamically; packed SDK writes and subsequent reads pass for CLI-created owners."
  "2026-11-06T06:25:39.515Z",codex-agent,"Final explanation audit found that nested derived values retained leaf quantities but omitted intermediate AST metadata, and shared dependency subgraphs could be revisited repeatedly. Replacing the walk with one deduplicated traversal, adding compact intermediate derivation witnesses, and adding a real-SDK shared-graph regression before final gates."
  "2026-11-06T06:50:15.886Z",codex-agent,"Nested explanations now include compact AST, operand-digest, declaration and limitation witnesses for every intermediate derivation, with each dependency quantity supplied once. A real-SDK graph of 22 derived nodes and 2 base observations requires 43 quantity reads and preserves all 21 intermediate formulas. Subtraction receives a distinct semantic kind and derived-kind identities retain the complete SHA-256. Focused core and edge checks passed 16 of 16; all 15 behavioral safeguard-removal proofs fail as expected and the restored implementation passes."
  "2026-11-06T07:22:39.554Z",claude-orchestrator,"Orchestrator manual test (2026-11-06, packed tarball, CLI 2026.11.5, a scratch project outside git). create, record x3 and compare/convert worked on real Sentry and telemetry numbers: count vs time refused dimension_mismatch, 2.7 s converted exactly to 9/200 min, and count to s refused. Gap: 'ms' was refused as unsupported_unit, although agents' test and latency figures are mostly in ms. Added the exact units ms (1/1000 s), kB, MB and GB (decimal), and GiB, with exact conversion tests (4560 ms = 114/25 s; 1 GiB = 16777216/15625 MB) and the README/ARCHITECTURE lists updated. Calendar units stay excluded by design. Cross-window comparison is tracked as pm-unit-2h1z."
